{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/251268-favorite-werewolf-antagonist-stories","id":251268,"title":"Favorite Werewolf Antagonist Stories","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-06T23:25:10-07:00","id":251268,"title":"Favorite Werewolf Antagonist Stories","content":"Figured I would create a thread to the unsung heroes of Werewolf campaigns everywhere...the antagonists.<br /> <br /> My favorite antagonist I ever created was a Greater Jaggling spirit of deception which convinced my players for more than 60 game sessions that it was a spirit of truth. Oh the fun I had when they began to believe everything it told them. Best deception ever was when it finally talked it's way into being the guardian of their locus and then convincing them all that it had somehow become weaker due to external influences (which they then killed in unknown fake retaliation). All the time it was just pocketing the extra essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T10:56:55-07:00","id":252484,"title":"","content":"My favorite antagonist in the Werewolf game I run just died last session. He was a 20 year-old skater Claimed by a ram spirit. When he first entered the players' territory, he was trying to escape a Predator King hunting party and was able to convince the PCs that he was a &quot;were-ram&quot; (other changing breeds had been a thing in this game before, so they were willing to roll with it). Pretty much as soon as they offered him sanctuary, they've hated him. He started dating the ritemaster's wolf-blooded apprentice, he hung out with the skater-punks (who thought his horns were a rad body mod), and started shaping their territory. He even called the werewolves &quot;moon-chained demons that ruin the shadow&quot; to their faces.<br /> His thing was &quot;strength through conflict&quot;, and he manipulated the high school and shaped the hiking trails to impose it on this happy tourist town.<br /> <br /> For almost a year (out of game), they've /hated/ &quot;goat boy&quot; - mocked and threatened him at every opportunity, but he never stepped out of line enough to justify killing him or running him off. Finally, he armed the football team with silver-tipped spears to have them fight a Predator King incursion - then took them on a hike through the spirit wilds as a final test on which ones should be Claimed. My players were <i>overjoyed</i> by the opportunity to kill him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 09-08-2014, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T12:29:45-07:00","id":252566,"title":"","content":"One stands out mostly due to chance. There was a beshilu, a rat man, who was chasing after us as we went on an attack against the Pure (who the beshilu of the city were allied with). It kept catching up to us (good rolls from it, bad from us), ahead of a massive swarm of beshilu and rats. Whenever we stopped to fight it, it ended up kicking us around until we had to run because the swarm was approaching. I'll always remember that one, the thing was like a ninja from an anime, hopping around through the trees and stopping just to beat us up.<br /> <br /> At one point we, needing allies against the overwhelming Pure presence, decided to find some of the more powerful hidden spirits of the city. We found some of them, but not one of the most promising ones, Bonegnasher. Bonegnasher was a sort of death/gator spirit formed from all the legends of alligators in the sewers. So we figured they'd be a great help if we could turn them to our side. Like I said we couldn't find him, however, and the game went on, our shadow-oriented members kept searching uselessly. After the premature climax of the story when we found the lair of the big bad and decided to just go after him, he tried to make an escape down a pit dug into the sewers (or the Shadow-version of the sewers). He had died from the fall (and the damage we inflicted). With his enslaved spirits going wild behind us we decided to use the dark passage to escape, and ran into a big, nasty spirit of some sort down there. We couldn't really see what was going on, since it was pitch black, and two of us stayed behind to try and fight it while the others escaped. Because of the darkness and it didn't really...act normally (breathe and stuff) we didn't even know when we killed it, ending up staying there, waiting in the dark, back to back and getting ready for it to attack again. Anyways, it turns out that was Bonegnasher.<br /> <br /> The majority of our antagonists were Pure, and it's really hard to narrow the 'favorite' ones down. There were a pair of Ivory Claws who were was a tricksy political animal, dominating the other Pure packs and often successfully manipulating Forsaken packs, the other was a gearhead and adrenaline junkie. They had a powerful totem that would shift circumstances to their benefit, providing every once and awhile they'd bet it all, so to speak, in risky scenarios. We had been toeing the Oaths of the Moon line in terms of killing their pack but didn't want to just do the deed when we finally subdued the gearhead, so we threw her in an abandoned meatlocker that was the center of a Wound. Which was bad. Avoiding breaking the Oaths of the Moon for us always ended up with us doing worse things. There was another pack, with territory right next to us, who had an angel as their totem, complete with flaming sword and handed down mandate to convert by the sword. They'd roam through the city, find wolf-blooded and stray wolves and bring them back to the church where they'd be tormented until they swore their loyalties to them. Whenever we saw them (pushing at the edge of our territory) they were wholesome looking wasps with Stepford smiles, looking at us like we had clocks on our faces counting down to the time to make the move to convert us. There was also this pack that, retrospectively I wanted to know more about. They mostly stuck to the subway tunnels, but were known as the Hiroshima Shadows and while small in number, were vicious. After the game I kept wondering what their totem was, exactly.<br /> <br /> Most of the games I've run have taken place in the same city. Years ago when I first started doing that, using some influences from DC's Gotham City and having gotten the Asylum bluebook I created Raker's Asylum (the name I took from elsewhere, I'm a big old thief) and had it run by a Bale Hound who uses it as the basis for her cult of personality among the psychiatric community as well as to experiment with patients (many of whom are wolf-blooded or otherwise touched by the supernatural). The players have gone there in every game, but have always avoided actually going inside. I've never been able to use her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-08-2014, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}